questions.question:
What does this print?
for i in range(5):
    if i == 2:
        continue
    if i == 4:
        break
    print(i)
else:
    print("else")

questions.answer:
continue skips 2 and break exits at 4, so 0, 1, 3 print and the else is skipped.

code:
for i in range(5):
    if i == 2:
        continue
    if i == 4:
        break
    print(i)
else:
    print("else")

